WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.350
Here's how this engine
works.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.400
You fill the burner case
with denatured alcohol

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.720
and attach the wick.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.000
You place the burner
case underneath the

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.050
heating cylinder.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.100
Light the wick.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.520
Let the engine preheat
for 10 to 15 seconds,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.700
then turn a flywheel to
kick start the engine.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.670
The flame heats the air
inside the heating

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.880
cylinder. The hot air
expands, moves into the

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.940
cooling cylinder, then
cools and contracts.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.760
This moves the working
piston up and down,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.960
turning the engine's
crankshaft.

